Subject: Use Fil-C zptrtable and pointer-typed rxres slots in Perl 5.40 core
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: Adopted and decomposed from pinned Fil-C (cede3de02b42:projects/perl-5.40.0). Perl's core encodes raw C pointers (XS/builtin/regex-engine/SvIV pointers) into IV integers via PTR2IV/INT2PTR and stores pointers inside UV arrays in pp_ctl.c (rxres_save/restore/free). Under Fil-C InvisiCaps, pointer-to-integer-to-pointer round-trips strip capabilities; this patch adds Perl_xsub_ptrtable / builtin_ptrtable using zptrtable_encode/zptrtable_decode, preserves pointer types in rxres slots, and uses memcpy in Perl_repeatcpy.
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: b14fce6d8d8a

